Pose and acceptance now follow the dressed-core ledger. The named candidate is not on disk yet, so the new report stays unverified and is not a finished knot.

**Scale.** When an annotation carries `scaleCalibration`, the similarity fit keeps the unconstrained pixels-per-metre reading and, if that scale falls outside 4250–5750, clamps it and recomputes the translation. Static acceptance uses that unconstrained reading on its own. A missing or malformed calibration cannot pass, and an oversized model stays a failed fit. Annotations without a calibration record still use the old unconstrained camera.

**Crossings.** `annotation.crossings` is scored from real projected segment intersections: reviewed role and material range, the nearer strand in the camera direction as over, and a position residual no larger than one nominal rope diameter. An unverified or missing binding stays unverified. Coordinates are not invented, and crossings are not copied into polylines.

**Extra rope.** `unexplainedVisible` now returns projected length, plus the sampling resolution. The locking-core box and known correspondence spans do not drop extra route. Only the frame edge, a traced centerline, the column, another rope in front, or an explicit hand mask can. Equal straight subdivisions measure the same length.

**Certificates.** `evaluateAcceptance` still reports the previous overall status and checks. It also reports `staticReconstruction`, `motionContinuity`, and `constructionCorrespondence` separately. Static pass needs tube, operations, calibrated scale, material totals and segments, positive gap, centerline, reviewed crossings, no extra length, and a reviewed source record supplied by the caller. Endpoint samples do not produce a motion pass.

**Report and viewer.** `scripts/evaluate-somerville-dressed.js` reads `data/somerville-final/dressed-candidate.json` and the static seed's own material coordinates. It writes `reports/somerville-dressed-report.json` and `reports/somerville-dressed-metadata.json`. Both currently say the candidate file is absent: static `UNVERIFIED`, motion `UNVERIFIED`, `finishedKnot: false`. Historical final JSON is unchanged. The viewer adds the dressed-candidate model, leaves the continuation candidate in place, enables final only when `acceptance.staticReconstruction.status` is `PASS`, and shows motion on its own badge. The core view frames the column while the full rope stays in the scene. Tube checks still run only when a model loads or changes.

`npm test` passed 109 tests and `npm run build` succeeded. In the browser, loose and loose-v2 loaded with their tube checks, the missing dressed file reported as not present, final stayed disabled, and the core view kept all 3500 loose-v2 points while aiming at the column.The preview server used for the viewer check has stopped. That was expected after the browser pass: loose and loose-v2 loaded, the missing dressed candidate was reported as not present, and the core view still drew the full rope. The pose and acceptance work is unchanged.
